From a19a9f1b605cf73f1aab498b15251593ed0f99df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:12:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: never turn off the output whose sound is in
 use

Without any file, an output that carries the sound of an audio output in use
(the previous commit: KODI::UTILS::CSoundOutputsInUse) is kept on as the outputs
of hades-keep-outputs are: on Kodi's device black, or as it was where the driver
does not take that (KEEP_OUTPUTS::KeepModes()); on another device as it was.

Which output, decided when the outputs that Kodi does not use are first turned
off, with every graphics device that drives a display
(KEEP_OUTPUTS::OutputsForSound(), CDRMUtils::DecideSoundOutputs()):

- the sound card is of a graphics device when it is another function of the
  same PCI device (NVIDIA, AMD, the graphics of an AMD processor), or when the
  graphics is a supplier of its controller (Intel, the i915 audio component);
- of the outputs of that device, the one whose EDID names the display that the
  ELD of the audio output names (maker, product, and name where both have one:
  KODI::UTILS::SameDisplay()). Two displays of one model are both kept.
- Wherever that is not certain (the engine has said nothing yet, the card is of
  no graphics device or not known, the display is not known, no output has it),
  every output that can carry sound (HDMI, DisplayPort, DVI) and has a display
  connected is kept on: of the card's device where that is known, else of all of
  them. That is what Kodi did before this build turned unused outputs off.
- An audio output that no graphics output carries (analog, S/PDIF, USB: ALSA
  gives its PCM no ELD) keeps nothing.

The turning off waits, 30 s at most, for the engine to say its outputs. What is
kept stays kept until Kodi ends. When the engine says other outputs later (the
user chose another audio output), the outputs that carry them are kept on from
then, and one of another device that was turned off comes back: that device is
given back to the console, which lights its outputs as when Kodi ends, and the
ones not kept on are turned off again. One of Kodi's own device does not: it has
no mode and nothing on it any more, lighting it is a mode set of another CRTC
in the commit of Kodi's frame, which can change the mode of Kodi's output too
and on amdgpu needs a picture that Kodi does not have; the log says so, and it
is on again (and kept) when Kodi starts again.

kodi.log, at info level:
  "/dev/dri/card0: HDMI-A-1 (DON AVR-X3800H (product 0x0041) on HDMI-A-1) stays
   on for the sound of 'ALSA:hdmi:CARD=PCH,DEV=0' (the audio output of the
   settings, the audio output in use): its ELD names DON AVR-X3800H (product
   0x0041), the display of this output"
  "... : not certain which output carries it (...): every output ... stays on (N)"
  "'ALSA:@:CARD=Generic,DEV=0' (...) plays to no graphics output (...): nothing
   is kept on for it"
  "the sound in use is on the output that Kodi draws on (HDMI-A-1): no other
   output is kept on for it"
and the lines of hades-keep-outputs say "(the sound in use)" for these outputs.

Tested on the host: the decision, the PCI matching, the identities, the published
list (75 checks; twelve mutations of the header, each caught); the tests of
hades-keep-outputs still pass (50). The rest is read and syntax-checked against
the build's own compile commands; what each machine gives, and what the receiver
hears, only hardware shows.
